{"id":"ear","name":"Ear","aliases":["Ear"],"sources":["nave","torrey","easton"],"topics":["nave:ear","torrey:ear-the"],"groups":["Figurative"],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Ear","text":"Used frequently in a figurative sense (Ps. 34:15). To “uncover the ear” is to show respect to a person (1 Sam. 20:2 marg.). To have the “ear heavy”, or to have “uncircumcised ears” (Isa. 6:10), is to be inattentive and disobedient. To have the ear “bored” through with an awl was a sign of perpetual servitude (Ex. 21:6)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H241","lemma":"אֹזֶן","xlit":"ʼôzen","gloss":"broadness. i.e. the ear","kjv":"advertise, audience, displease, ear","count":36,"share":0.73},{"strong":"H8571","lemma":"תְּנוּךְ","xlit":"tᵉnûwk","gloss":"a pinnacle","kjv":"tip","count":6,"share":0.12},{"strong":"H931","lemma":"בֹּהֶן","xlit":"bôhen","gloss":"the thumb of the hand or great toe of the foot","kjv":"thumb, great toe","count":6,"share":0.12},{"strong":"H3233","lemma":"יְמָנִי","xlit":"yᵉmânîy","gloss":"right","kjv":"right","count":6,"share":0.12},{"strong":"H238","lemma":"אָזַן","xlit":"ʼâzan","gloss":"to broaden out the ear","kjv":"give  ear, hear. See H239","count":6,"share":0.12},{"strong":"H7272","lemma":"רֶגֶל","xlit":"regel","gloss":"a foot","kjv":"be able to endure, according as, after, coming","count":6,"share":0.12}],"verses":["Exod.21.6","Exod.29.20","Lev.8.23","Lev.14.14","Lev.14.17","Lev.14.25","Lev.14.28","Deut.15.17","Job.12.11","Job.13.1","Job.29.11","Job.33.16","Job.36.10","Ps.17.6","Ps.40.6","Ps.58.4","Ps.94.9","Prov.2.2","Prov.5.1","Prov.15.31","Prov.18.15","Prov.20.12","Prov.21.13","Prov.25.12","Prov.28.9","Eccl.1.8","Isa.6.10","Isa.30.21","Isa.35.5","Isa.43.8","Jer.6.10","Jer.7.24","Jer.9.20","Jer.35.15","Ezek.16.12","Zech.7.11","Exod.15.26","Exod.21.5","Ps.39.12","Ps.77.1","Ps.80.1","Ps.84.8","Isa.1.10","Isa.43.10","Hos.2.13","Matt.13.15","Matt.13.16","Acts.7.51","2Tim.4.3"],"related":[{"id":"deafness","type":"seealso","why":"Nave's Topical Bible lists it